    deepExplanation: "Step 1 — Define the node:\n```ts\ninterface TreeNode {\n  value: number;\n  left: TreeNode | null;\n  right: TreeNode | null;\n}\n```\n\nStep 2 — WITHOUT BUILT-IN / CORE:\n```ts\ninterface TreeNode {\n  value: number;\n  left: TreeNode | null;\n  right: TreeNode | null;\n}\n\nfunction createNode(value: number): TreeNode {\n  return {\n    value,\n    left: null,\n    right: null,\n  };\n}\n\nfunction countNodes(root: TreeNode | null): number {\n  if (root === null) return 0;\n\n  return 1 + countNodes(root.left) + countNodes(root.right);\n}\n```\n\nStep 3 — WITH BUILT-IN-friendly array representation:\n```ts\ninterface TreeNode {\n  value: number;\n  left: TreeNode | null;\n  right: TreeNode | null;\n}\n\nfunction levelOrderValues(root: TreeNode | null): number[] {\n  if (root === null) return [];\n\n  const queue: TreeNode[] = [root];\n  const values: number[] = [];\n  let front = 0;\n\n  while (front < queue.length) {\n    const node = queue[front++]!;\n    values.push(node.value);\n\n    if (node.left !== null) queue.push(node.left);\n    if (node.right !== null) queue.push(node.right);\n  }\n\n  return values;\n}\n```\n\nStep 4 — Example:\n```text\n      1\n     /     2   3\n```\nThe root is 1, left child is 2, right child is 3.\nNode count = 3.\n\nComplexity:\ncountNodes = O(n) time and O(h) recursion stack, where h is tree height.",
